{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791564665,"nonce":"hKvjT1RQyDV021TNZe6lVzg5zr4=","message":"Step 1 landed in c8fc5ae: src/css, a port of ashui's CssParser, Selector, Stylesheet and Media parsing (nesting, @media, @import through a loader, mixins, @keyframes, :root variables, diagnostics with file, line and column), the compiled format (css::compiled, BCSS version 1: a string table, then the sheet; decode refuses other versions and malformed bytes), css::json (one canonical JSON shape), and the blinc-css command (build with --no-default-features --features css-cli; -o writes compiled bytes, --json, --classes; exit 1 on errors).\n\nParity with ashui: 47 sheets (ashui's user-agent sheet, components.css, media.css, the demo and fixture sheets, 33 inline sheets from ashui's CSS tests, and two edge-case sheets of rare syntax and every error path) give identical JSON from ashui's Haxe parser and from blinc-css, rules, specificity, declarations, media, positions and diagnostics alike. The only difference was float formatting (Haxe's interpreter prints 17 digits), the same value.\n\nKept from blinc_css: nothing yet. Its selector model has five state pseudo-classes and no attribute selectors, and its parser writes values into Blinc's typed ElementStyle, so the parse layer follows ashui's instead.\n\nNext: selector matching and cascade on LayoutContext, writing through the owned property routing that blinc_ts added in 88b8c7f; that needs the value readers (ashui's CssValue and Properties) in Rust as well.","files":null}]}